this is basically a soap opera for great  apes silly as it seems researchers made  videos like this to show that non-human  Apes can recognize that others may have  false beliefs it's part of research  investigating theory of mind which asked  questions like what do great apes like  chimps bonobos and orangutangs think  about other's minds humans do this all  the time we think about what others are  thinking their goals intentions  expectations and beliefs even false ones  but it was thought only people could  understand someone else had the wrong  idea about something this experiment was  set up the test if other primates could  do this  the subjects watched a drama play out  and their eye movements are tracked to  see what they expect the players to do  they sip juice from a fixed straw which  holds them still enough that their gaze  can be tracked the dramatic conflict in  the soap opera keeps the primates  interested they need to be invested  enough to closely watch the scene adding  an ape-like creature reminiscent of King  Kong and some social conflict was just  enough to keep their attention here's  what happens in an ape soap opera step  by step first the human shows interest  in Iraq note the chimp observer in the  upper left-hand corner of the screen its  eyes are being tracked through this  entire process then the mysterious  primate comes in it takes the rock  making a lot of noise as it does though  the red dots show the chimp is watching  the scene intently the human and the  chimp both watch the mystery primate  hide the rock on to the left box then  the human suddenly leaves while the  human is gone  chimp watches the rock being moved the  red dots show all these motions are  being tracked until finally the rock is  removed all together the chimp sees the  person coming back into the room and  reaching for the boxes where does the  chimp think the person is going to look  for the rock according to its gaze the  chimp looks on the left even though it  knows the rock is gone in a series of  these trials all three species of apes  tested orangutangs chimps and bonobos  looked where they thought the human  would go suggesting that these Apes  recognized a false belief in another  mind according to this research  non-human Apes appear to understand that  individuals have unique perceptions  about the world the person doesn't know  the rock is gone so the ape looks where  they think the person thinks it is this  finding suggests that these Apes to have  some understanding of what's happening  in another individuals mind and  threatens to tip theory of mind off the  human only pedestal  you  you
 

